==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|paper|work}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpeɪ.pɚˌwɝk/|/ˈpeɪ.pɚ.wɚk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paperwork.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# [[routine]] [[work]] involving [[written]] [[document]]s
#: {{coi|en|do '''paperwork'''}}
# [[written]] [[document]]s
# {{lb|en|hyperbolic}} [[excessive]] paperwork, [[busy work]], [[red tape]].
# {{lb|en|US|prison slang}} [[court|Court]] [[document]]s or [[presentencing|pre-sentencing]] [[investigation]] [[report]]s detailing the [[prisoner]]'s [[criminal]] [[history]] {{gloss|usually in the context of discerning whether an inmate has been charged for sex-related [[offense]]s or is likely to be an [[informant]]}}.
#: {{coi|en|to have bad '''paperwork'''|to be charged with sex-related offenses or to likely be an informant}}

